{"sent":"On Oct 4, 2026 at about 6:40 pm I slipped on a wet floor near the milk fridge at a Circle K in Ottawa. There was no wet-floor sign. I fell on my right hip. A shopper, Sam Patel, saw it. The manager wrote notes. I went to the hospital that night; X-rays showed a bad bruise, no break. I missed 3 days of work (Oct 5 to 7) at $150 a day and bought Tylenol and an ice pack for $18.45. I want to claim $5,000 for pain and suffering, $450 lost wages and $18.45 for medicine.

I am the one bringing this case.

Nothing has been filed with a court yet.","chosen":null}

